; Font index: one word per character $20-$7F, giving the glyph offset and width
;
; Word n belongs to the character with code $20+n (the word of character c is at $6130+2*(c-$20)). Read by the
; character printer #R$9E79 and by #R$9F52, which measures a string in the proportional font.
; .
; Word layout (stored low byte first): bits 0-11: offset from the address of the word's high byte (its own address +
; 1) to the glyph in #R$61F0; bits 12-15: glyph width in pixels minus 2 (GLYPH_WIDTH_BIAS), so the glyphs are 2-17
; pixels wide. The width is also the advance to the next character.
@label=FontIndex
